From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phil Rodgers <philip.rodgers@glasgow.ac.uk>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:00:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add a WASI backend

On `target_os = "wasi"` the host supplies the terminal through the
`crossterm_host` imports: `terminal_size()` and a blocking
`read_input(buf, len, timeout_ms)`, which returns bytes, 0 on timeout or
-2 after a resize. `terminal/sys/wasi.rs` implements size and raw mode
(a flag only); `event/source/wasi.rs` feeds input bytes to the unix ANSI
parser and turns a resize into `Event::Resize`.
